<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Black Seminoles</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Seminole Maroons</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Black Seminoles were people of African descent, many of them escaped slaves from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> and the Carolinas, who lived alongside the Seminole in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>. They kept their own villages, paid tribute to Seminole leaders and fought with them against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. After removal some settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-territory">Indian Territory</a>, while others moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/black-seminoles.jpg" alt="Black Seminoles" width="320" height="377" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: State Library and Archives of Florida · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aged_black_Seminole_smokes_from_his_pipe-_Everglades,_Florida_(3311787651).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
